Give `default_to_tsc_transpiler` universal scope so it reaches the exec configuration.

Bazel 10 flips `--incompatible_exclude_starlark_flags_from_exec_config`, which resets Starlark
flags to their defaults in the exec configuration. A `ts_project` built as a tool then fails
analysis with "Required Transpiler Selection" even though the flag is set.
See https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/26909.

Independent of the other patches. Kept separate so it can go upstream.

diff --git a/ts/BUILD.bazel b/ts/BUILD.bazel
--- a/ts/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/ts/BUILD.bazel
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 bool_flag(
     name = "default_to_tsc_transpiler",
     build_setting_default = False,
+    scope = "universal",
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
